\title{Bi-invertible Map}
\taxon{Definition}
\import{macros}
\p{
    A map #{f:A\to B} is \strong{bi-invertible} if it has both a
    [section](def-005G) and a [retraction](def-005H), or equivalently a separate
    [right and left inverse](def-005A). Define
    ##{
        \mathsf{isBiInv}(f)
        \defeq
        \mathsf{sec}(f)\times\mathsf{retr}(f).
    }
    The left and right inverse maps are supplied independently; their inverse
    laws imply that they are homotopic.
}
